Chapter: EmptyLiteral

 A9. The literal on the first line opens at end of line and is silently "",
 and so is the lone quote closing it. Both vanish; no diagnostic is raised.
 Expected "a<newline>", emitted `cx_concat(cx_concat("a", n), "")`.

 One character before the newline -- `"a" & n & "b` then a closing quote --
 halts with CDX7 instead, which is the finding: the rule exists and only the
 empty case skips it. It is not in this file because it would stop the file
 compiling, and what is worth running is the half that does not complain.

  silent : Text -> Text
  silent (n) = "a" & n & "
"

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-text (silent "x")
    print-text "END"
  end
